      "writtenOn": "2022-08-12T18:26:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "RuleBuilder already has PathForOutput, having SboxOutputPath is going to be confusing.  I think instead the metalava code should keep around a path to the sbox output directory and use Join on it to create whatever paths it needs.",
      "revId": "3497efc0eda1c708d2395171edd12d00cff72078",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5dc51649_7a71bdd5",
        "filename": "android/rule_builder.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 155,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-12T18:43:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could but then I have to pass that base directory around alongside the rule/command. e.g. to stubsFlags(). Which seems redundant given that it is already encapsulated within the rule.\n\nAlso, I was thinking that in future all users of the Sbox could be switched to this approach and then Sbox could be made safer/simpler to use by having it always create a sub-directory within the output directory so that it was harder for users to accidentally create other rules which output into the Sbox output directory.\n\nFTR - metalava did that without my changes, e.g. the update and check timestamps were created in the Sbox output directory and deleted by Sbox. I don\u0027t know if that caused any actually issues but it did make it much harder to work out what was happening.\n\nMaybe a better name would help?",
      "parentUuid": "77ccf01a_46c5cf80",
      "revId": "3497efc0eda1c708d2395171edd12d00cff72078",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dcb4a577_1943cbf8",
        "filename": "android/rule_builder.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 155,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-12T22:35:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could store the directory in the Droidstubs struct where it would be available to all of those calls.\n\nI agree that using a subdirectory would be safer, but I worry that having sbox create a subdirectory is going to export that implementation detail into all the tests.  You didn\u0027t want to move the checked metalava output files because they were referenced in tests, but this would require moving every output of every sbox rule.\n\nA better name would always help, but there are so many directories and different ways to refer to the same directory from inside and outside the sandbox that it\u0027s never going to be completely obvious from the name what is going on.",
      "parentUuid": "5dc51649_7a71bdd5",
      "revId": "3497efc0eda1c708d2395171edd12d00cff72078",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
